WEBVTT

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.430
Are you alright, Mr. Joestar?

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.570
Yes... thank you, Avdol.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:48.000
It's a old memory, but I just don't feel
comfortable being in an airplane.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.870
As I told you before,
remember, it's fifty days.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:54.070
If we can't confront Dio
within fifty days, then...

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:58.510
I know.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:01.450
Holley's life will be in danger.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.190
Wha...? What was that?

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:22.110
Joestar-san! The left-
side engine is on fire!

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.980
Calm down!
Everyone, remain seated!

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.780
But, Joestar-san! The engine...!

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:33.310
Don't worry. I'll go ask them
what happened myself!

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:39.680
Captain!

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:41.960
Tell me what's happened!

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.030
I don't know!

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.530
We're rapidly losing altitude!

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.020
We're out of control!

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.130
Please return to your seat!

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:51.260
If this continues, we'll
crash into the ocean!

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.130
W... What?

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.340
What a pain...

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:32.980
In any case, I'm glad
everyone is okay.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.440
Many ships travel back and
forth through this area.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:38.640
They'll hear our distress signal
and will surely come to our rescue.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:40.940
I sure hope so.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:44.150
We can't waste our
time in a place like this.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.790
But... if this accident was
caused by our enemy...

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.470
Well, I guess we're not
out of luck just yet!

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:11.420
Signal...

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:45.040
Good, now we can continue on.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:47.780
I guess we shouldn't take
my good luck lightly.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:53.590
What's wrong, Avdol-san?

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:58.090
The ramp has been lowered, but why
isn't anyone showing themselves?

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:32.690
I guess no one's
coming to greet us.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.970
Where is the crew?

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.960
It's just like the Mary Celeste, which
disappeared in Bermuda, isn't it?

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.540
Hey! Isn't anyone here?

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:52.750
...anyone here?

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.720
In any case, let's
investigate this ship.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:16.340
Something wrong?

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.480
Look at this window.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.840
How could they have
spotted us through this...!?

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.490
No one in the Engine Room either.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.330
So, there's no one on board...?

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:46.300
What was that...

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:47.440
just now?

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:50.470
Joestar-san! Is something wrong?

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.040
There was a sound from inside.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:08.360
What a huge monkey.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:14.600
This is an orangutan.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.230
Is he telling us to open it?

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:24.110
So it would seem...

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:33.720
Oh ho...!

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.980
Pretty smart for a monkey.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:37.480
Be careful!

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.460
An orangutan has five times
the strength of a human,

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:42.590
so he could easily
rip your arm off.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:48.500
Well, this means there must be
someone around to feed him, at least.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.600
Let's go. We should be
able to find his owner.

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:11.620
What the...?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.030
Look at the bridge!

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:37.680
So this is a ghost ship after all.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:39.010
Ridiculous!

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:52.760
Let's go.

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:54.970
I think it's best if
we all stay together.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:58.460
What do you think...

00:10:59.140 --> 00:10:59.830
everyone?

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.060
This ship is dangerous.

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:04.330
What can we do now, in
the middle of the ocean?

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:08.150
But, we don't even know
where we're sailing yet...

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.350
What's that...?

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:17.620
I guess we'll have to go see.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:53.230
Bonjour, Monsieur Joestar's party.

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:56.100
You!?

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:56.900
Wait...

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:02.780
How did you know about us?

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:10.020
A man with a birthmark
shaped like this told me.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:16.650
Another one...?

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:21.490
Joestar-san!

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:22.160
Look out!

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:25.670
What!?

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:37.610
What!?

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:42.750
My Stand's name is Silver Chariot...

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:44.890
It seems, Avdol...

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:46.660
that you want to be killed.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.660
I made a clock out
of fire on that table.

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:55.170
Before it burns twelve
o'clock, I will kill you.

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:57.900
Such formidable swordplay.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.400
Truly amazing.

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:03.340
But, you said you would
kill me by twelve o'clock?

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:06.450
Don't you think you're
being too vain...

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:08.140
man from France?

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:10.340
My greeting is overdue.

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:12.010
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:14.340
My name is Polnareff.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:15.650
Jean-Pierre...

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:17.080
Polnareff.

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:19.150
Merci beaucoup.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:21.450
My sincere thanks for
your self-introduction.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.390
Now then!

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.700
When Avdol's Stand
moved his arm,

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:29.030
the lower half of the
table burned away!

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:34.660
I don't want you to think my
fire is like a natural flame.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:39.400
Because it can control fire at
will, it is called Magician's Red.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:41.570
Well done!

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:42.750
But...

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:45.980
awhile ago, you said
that I was too vain...

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:48.840
about my swordplay?

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:55.830
Too vain, you said?

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.290
Can you still say that after this?

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:00.700
Amazing!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.700
He pierced five coins
with one thrust.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:05.800
No, take a good look...

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:07.300
That's not all...

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:12.070
I see.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:16.040
So you understand
what this means.

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:19.640
My Stand can cut fire
with complete control.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:23.650
In other words, you are
virtually powerless against me.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:27.580
When did he...!?

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:34.800
I could kill you
right here, Avdol...

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.530
but isn't it true that
a more open space...

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:39.160
would enable you to use
your ability at full power?

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:43.800
Beating you there would be a more
suitable victory for my Stand.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:45.810
Everyone, get in line!

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:48.570
Openly, squarely, and in
order... I will cut you apart!

00:14:58.990 --> 00:14:59.920
Avdol...

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:03.260
Mr. Joestar, let me
handle this myself.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:06.160
Just as he said, with
this much open space,

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:09.500
I can more freely
use my Stand.

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:11.600
A prediction...

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:15.740
You will destroy yourself
with your own Stand.

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:27.220
What happened to
your vaunted flame?

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:29.520
If you're not going to
breathe fire, then I will begin!

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.900
He made a fool out of him.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.530
He was waiting for
Magician's Red to breathe fire!

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:51.740
You don't stand a
chance against me.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:56.850
He's coming.
For real, this time.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:04.150
Oh boy... I don't want
to get broiled by that.

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:07.660
Cross Fire Hurricane!

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:12.590
Is that all the
power you've got?

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:15.460
If so...!

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:21.540
The flame was too powerful...
he's burning himself!

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:23.770
Just as I said, right?

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.040
Mr. Avdol...

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:29.280
Ahhh... a desperate struggle, huh?

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:32.990
<i>What is this resistance...? </i>

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.250
Once again!

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:37.920
Cross Fire!

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.360
His Stand is melting.

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:46.300
He's badly burned.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:48.400
If he's lucky, he's only
severely injured. No...

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:51.070
perhaps I should
say, if he's unlucky.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:53.600
In any case, he won't be able
to stand up for three months.

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:56.200
His Stand has been melted,
and is unable to fight.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.540
Well, Mr. Joestar...

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:03.380
let's discuss how
we will get to Egypt.

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:08.380
Over there!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:10.390
What!?

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:15.790
I can't believe it!

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:17.990
Bravo!

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:19.890
Oh, bravo!

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.130
Why is his body
floating in mid-air!?

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:27.800
Look closely with
your Stand's eyes.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:30.970
His Stand!

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:37.710
This... is Silver Chariot
without his armor.

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:41.980
You seem to be
appropriately amazed.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:43.810
If you don't mind...

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:46.220
kindly explain what happened.

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:47.390
Good.

00:17:47.490 --> 00:17:49.760
Your attitude is
most commendable.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.930
The explosion earlier was not
my Stand being blown to bits...

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:56.160
but the impact of my Stand
throwing off his armor.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:01.070
Only his armor was
burned by your fire...

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:03.610
so I was able to get by
with only minor injuries.

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:07.440
And now, with the armor
gone, I can move even faster.

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:10.550
So you're saying that because
of the weight of your armor,

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.550
you couldn't avoid my
Cross Fire Hurricane?

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.020
Oui.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:16.550
That's right.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.650
Which means, without
your protective armor,

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:22.290
if you're struck by my CFH
again, you will not survive.

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:25.450
Oui. But that is impossible...

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:26.730
Impossible?

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:31.340
Because I am about to show you
something that will horrify you.

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:34.340
What!?

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:35.340
It can't be!

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.310
There should be only
one Stand per person!

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.710
You seem horrified.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:43.040
This afterimage affects
not just the visual senses,

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:44.780
but the physical
senses as well.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:47.810
How about this swordplay!?

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.660
That was an afterimage.

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:57.960
Your stunts are now
useless against my Stand.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:02.760
Avdol!

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:07.040
Actually...

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:10.700
a variation exists for my CFH.

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:13.780
The ankh-shaped fire
usually forms a single flame,

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.780
but I can split it up and
hurl it as many flames!

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:26.290
Really, Avdol!

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:30.560
Not good! His Stands
have formed a circle!

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:32.930
Once again, he'll simply
strike the flames back.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:36.270
Easy, easy, easy, easy, easy!

00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:42.070
I will strike them back!

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:46.740
What!?

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:59.050
That's the hole his Stand made
when he struck Avdol's flames back!

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:04.090
I see.

00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:07.590
He made use of a hole that was
made in the middle of battle.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:11.800
Being able to split his flames
made this strategy possible.

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:23.410
Burning to death must be painful.

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:26.080
Use that blade to end your life.

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:46.070
I was vain...

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:49.870
thinking my swordplay would
never be beaten by mere flames.

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:53.940
I choose to burn
to death gracefully.

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:58.910
Consider it a salute to your ability
from the one who lost the battle.

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:04.990
His proud spirit goes
beyond Dio's orders...

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:09.820
this man who remains true to the
code of honor you call, "chivalry."

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:13.760
If we let him die like this,
we may regret it later.

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:18.230
Perhaps there's a good reason behind
him becoming one of Dio's assassins.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:24.830
We're safe now! Our enemy
has been struck down.

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:29.180
So I see. Honestly, you really
had me worried for a while.

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:30.440
That's great!

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:37.050
Watch out!

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:50.930
Look out! Hit the deck!

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:18.720
That damned... is he a Stand user?

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:25.400
He turned a bolt into a pipe...

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:26.470
Jotaro!

00:22:29.980 --> 00:22:32.240
Jotaro... The ship itself is also...!

00:22:33.010 --> 00:22:34.140
a Stand!?

00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:47.160
You stinkin' ape...

00:22:47.760 --> 00:22:49.460
Now it's your turn!

00:22:59.610 --> 00:23:00.470
Jotaro!

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:09.770
Star Finger!

00:23:16.260 --> 00:23:17.220
Jotaro!

00:23:46.750 --> 00:23:48.780
It seems to be over now...

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:57.660
But whether this boat will break down
or reach land first is anyone's guess.

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:01.800
Who would have imagined his
Stand used a little boat like this...?

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:06.130
If we'd known this would happen, we
would have tried to tame that monkey!

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:12.940
To think he was so heavily
damaged... he's quite something.

00:24:13.350 --> 00:24:16.910
He must have something
he has to accomplish...

00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:20.150
Otherwise, no matter
how young he is...

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:22.280
it would have been impossible
to recover so quickly!

00:24:24.060 --> 00:24:25.420
Monsieur Joestar!

00:24:27.260 --> 00:24:28.780
I may be prying,

00:24:28.930 --> 00:24:30.950
but you always
have your gloves on.

00:24:31.630 --> 00:24:34.660
Don't tell me your left
hand is a right hand!

00:24:34.770 --> 00:24:36.600
My left hand... a right hand?

00:24:36.900 --> 00:24:38.890
What a strange question to ask!

00:24:39.340 --> 00:24:42.900
I've... been looking for a man
whose hands are both right hands.

00:24:49.420 --> 00:24:52.910
This is an honorable wound I
received in battle fifty years ago.

00:24:53.450 --> 00:24:55.390
My apologies. Please forgive me.

00:24:56.820 --> 00:24:59.520
Polnareff, what's this all about?

00:25:00.230 --> 00:25:03.630
I've been looking for a man
who killed my younger sister...

00:25:05.830 --> 00:25:08.130
It happened three years ago...

00:25:13.340 --> 00:25:16.370
That day, my sister was
walking home from school...

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:19.310
...together with a classmate.

00:25:41.900 --> 00:26:06.330
Noooooo!

00:26:06.890 --> 00:26:08.190
I don't know his face.

00:26:08.630 --> 00:26:11.430
But, his hands are
both right hands.

00:26:12.160 --> 00:26:14.530
Obviously a man
with a Stand ability.

00:26:17.170 --> 00:26:18.360
I made a vow...

00:26:18.640 --> 00:26:22.470
that for the dignity of my sister's soul,
I'll make him atone with his death.

00:26:26.710 --> 00:26:28.270
Then, one year ago...

00:26:28.780 --> 00:26:30.680
I met Dio.

00:26:36.090 --> 00:26:37.180
W-who are you?

00:26:37.790 --> 00:26:42.590
I can see a man, boldly
confronting you in your mind.

00:26:42.930 --> 00:26:46.690
Listen, how about you
and I become friends?

00:26:46.900 --> 00:26:51.560
If you will help me with my
work, I will lend you a hand.

00:26:52.200 --> 00:26:55.070
Perhaps I can find
that man for you.

00:26:56.080 --> 00:26:59.170
So, I was ordered to kill you all.

00:27:00.110 --> 00:27:02.510
Even though I knew it was
a whisper from the devil...

00:27:03.150 --> 00:27:06.980
I'd made a deal to get the information
I needed to avenge my sister.

00:27:07.990 --> 00:27:11.620
He's good at taking advantage
of someone's weaknesses.

00:27:11.760 --> 00:27:14.190
But, based on what
you told us just now,

00:27:14.290 --> 00:27:17.520
Dio already knew that man.

00:27:17.760 --> 00:27:18.560
What...!?

00:27:19.570 --> 00:27:20.330
Polnareff...

00:27:20.570 --> 00:27:22.030
what are you going to do now?

00:27:23.340 --> 00:27:25.630
I'm going with you guys!

00:27:26.270 --> 00:27:29.730
If I go after Dio, I might be able to
meet the man who killed my sister.

00:27:30.280 --> 00:27:31.800
Alright, then!

00:27:32.280 --> 00:27:34.870
Even though our goals may be different,
we're heading to the same destination!

00:27:36.980 --> 00:27:40.180
It's decided... let's hurry
up and get to Egypt!

00:27:40.520 --> 00:27:42.110
I'm gonna have fun!

00:27:42.220 --> 00:27:44.160
The Egyptian women
are very mysterious.

00:27:44.260 --> 00:27:46.020
That's what makes them so
appealing, don't you think?

00:27:47.760 --> 00:27:50.350
I thought he was a man
filled with chivalry...

00:27:50.500 --> 00:27:52.660
but now I'm not so sure.

00:27:53.130 --> 00:27:55.360
His mood certainly
changes in a hurry.

00:27:55.900 --> 00:27:59.500
His mind and his instincts seem
to be completely independent.

00:28:01.610 --> 00:28:03.170
What a pain...

00:28:14.150 --> 00:28:15.450
Strength...

00:28:15.520 --> 00:28:17.580
so useless.

00:28:17.720 --> 00:28:19.020
Not only that, even the Chariot...

00:28:19.160 --> 00:28:21.630
Polnareff, double-crossed us...

00:28:24.400 --> 00:28:28.330
But all the cards of
destiny are in my hands...

00:28:32.710 --> 00:28:35.000
Don't let it trouble you, Lord Dio.

00:28:35.110 --> 00:28:38.240
Even if those useless
worms defect to the enemy,

00:28:38.340 --> 00:28:41.310
they are no match
for your power...

00:28:41.650 --> 00:28:46.410
The Emperor and The Hanged Man
are already on their way to India...

00:28:46.820 --> 00:28:48.220
One of them will do it.

00:28:48.320 --> 00:28:53.160
The Hanged Man's right hands
will take care of them for sure.

00:28:54.060 --> 00:28:55.120
Because...!

00:28:55.360 --> 00:28:59.460
He is the Master of the invincible
Stand, The Hanged Man!

00:28:59.570 --> 00:29:02.400
And is my precious,
dearest son as well!

00:29:02.540 --> 00:29:04.530
His name is J. Gail...!
